# Ansible Testing Rules

## Molecule is Mandatory
Every role has a `molecule/default/` directory before any task is written.
No role ships without Molecule tests. No exceptions.

Directory structure required at role init:
```
molecule/
  default/
    molecule.yml    — driver config, platforms, provisioner
    converge.yml    — playbook that applies the role
    verify.yml      — assertions about end state
```

## Test Lifecycle
Run the full Molecule lifecycle and ensure all phases pass:
```
molecule create       — spin up test container/VM
molecule converge     — run converge.yml (apply the role)
molecule idempotence  — run converge.yml again; fail if changed > 0
molecule verify       — run verify.yml assertions
molecule destroy      — tear down test container/VM
molecule test         — run all of the above in sequence
```
All phases must pass before merging a role change.

## Idempotence Test
Molecule's built-in idempotence check (`molecule idempotence`) runs the role a second time.
The second run must show:
```
PLAY RECAP
instance  :  ok=N  changed=0  unreachable=0  failed=0  skipped=0
```
Any `changed > 0` is a test failure. Common fixes:
- Use `creates:` parameter on `command` tasks
- Add `when:` conditions based on registered facts
- Replace `shell`/`command` with idempotent modules

## Verify with Ansible Tasks
Prefer Ansible verify tasks for simplicity. Use `ansible.builtin.assert` + `ansible.builtin.service_facts` + `ansible.builtin.uri`:
```yaml
- name: Gather service facts
  ansible.builtin.service_facts:

- name: Assert nginx is running
  ansible.builtin.assert:
    that:
      - ansible_facts.services['nginx.service'].state == 'running'
    fail_msg: "nginx service is not running"

- name: Assert nginx responds on configured port
  ansible.builtin.uri:
    url: "http://localhost:{{ nginx_port }}"
    status_code: 200
```
Use Testinfra (Python pytest plugin) only for complex assertions not expressible in Ansible.

## Docker Driver for Most Roles
Fast iteration. Use pre-configured images:
- Ubuntu 24.04: `geerlingguy/docker-ubuntu2404-ansible`
- Ubuntu 22.04: `geerlingguy/docker-ubuntu2204-ansible`
- CentOS/RHEL: `geerlingguy/docker-rockylinux9-ansible`

Standard molecule.yml:
```yaml
dependency:
  name: galaxy
driver:
  name: docker
platforms:
  - name: instance
    image: geerlingguy/docker-ubuntu2404-ansible
    pre_build_image: true
provisioner:
  name: ansible
verifier:
  name: ansible
```

## Vagrant Driver
Use only for roles that require:
- systemd (real init system, not Docker's stub)
- Kernel modules (`modprobe`, iptables, etc.)
- Real network interfaces
- SELinux/AppArmor enforcement

Vagrant tests are slower — run them in a separate CI job, not the default pipeline.
